South Africa head coach Hugo Broos called on his defeated squad to leave the World Cup with a sense of achievement despite losing their first game in the knockout stages to Canada.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1a86ea8c-734f-11f1-aa41-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/hugo-bross.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1a86ea8c-734f-11f1-aa41-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/hugo-bross.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9035c00a-734a-11f1-bb57-41cd7e4b9208</guid><pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 00:31:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1a86ea8c-734f-11f1-aa41-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/hugo-bross.jpg">AFP - ETIENNE LAURENT</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>European heatwave continues to top records amid high alerts in the east</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260627-european-heatwave-continues-to-top-records-amid-high-alerts-in-the-east</link><description>
Tens of millions face a weekend of extreme temperatures in Europe as a deadly heatwave moves eastwards, with German forecasters warning that more records could be broken and eastern countries issuing a slew of red alerts for the coming days.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/90fa4050-713e-11f1-9bde-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-25T151834Z-985103065-RC231MAW2D7O-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-HEAT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/90fa4050-713e-11f1-9bde-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-25T151834Z-985103065-RC231MAW2D7O-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-HEAT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">beea3ec0-7242-11f1-9935-6f8bbe7fb1bc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 16:10:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/90fa4050-713e-11f1-9bde-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-25T151834Z-985103065-RC231MAW2D7O-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-HEAT.jpg">REUTERS - Gonzalo Fuentes</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Marine biobanks: the science of 'stopping time' for an ecosystem under pressure</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260627-marine-biobanks-the-science-of-stopping-time-for-an-ocean-under-pressure</link><description>
In labs around the world, the ocean is being kept in jars. Some of it is alive, bubbling in flasks, while some lies frozen in liquid nitrogen. These marine biobanks are collections of coral cells, algae, bacteria and other living materials that scientists are working to preserve before warming seas and disappearing habitats consume them.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e0533e84-7168-11f1-afd3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Copyright-EMBRC-Spain-ECIMAT-Experimental-facilities-5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e0533e84-7168-11f1-afd3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Copyright-EMBRC-Spain-ECIMAT-Experimental-facilities-5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ce2604a-6f14-11f1-98fc-7525a4f77d89</guid><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 10:18:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e0533e84-7168-11f1-afd3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Copyright-EMBRC-Spain-ECIMAT-Experimental-facilities-5.jpg">© EMBRC Spain/ECIMAT</source><dc:creator>Amanda Morrow</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Wissa the wizard as DRC conjure up first trip to World Cup knockout stages</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260628-wissa-the-wizard-as-drc-conjure-up-first-trip-to-world-cup-knockout-stages</link><description>
Yoane Wissa scored two goals on Saturday night in Atlanta as Democratic Republic of Congo staged a second half rally to beat Uzbekistan 3-1 and advance to the knockout stages at the World Cup for the first time.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c97f91ee-729e-11f1-873f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/wiiss.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c97f91ee-729e-11f1-873f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/wiiss.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">25f6aa62-729e-11f1-a970-71c6c1951f4c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 28 Jun 2026 03:41:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c97f91ee-729e-11f1-873f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/wiiss.jpg">AP Photo/Erik S. Lesser - Erik S. Lesser</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Croatia outmuscle Ghana to take second place in Group L as England beat Panama</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260628-croatia-outmuscle-ghana-to-take-second-place-in-group-l-as-england-beat-panama-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Croatia saw off Ghana 2-1 on Saturday night at the Philadelphia Stadium to claim the runners-up spot in Group L behind England who overcame Panama 2-0 in New Jersey.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e455208-729a-11f1-9eab-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/susic.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e455208-729a-11f1-9eab-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/susic.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa5e3862-7288-11f1-ab8c-979b41aa7e93</guid><pubDate>Sun, 28 Jun 2026 02:43:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e455208-729a-11f1-9eab-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/susic.jpg">REUTERS - Pilar Olivares</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>'A wake up call': Municipal misery hangs over upcoming South African elections</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260628-municipal-misery-weighs-on-looming-south-african-elections-november-anc-da-black-townships</link><description>
Mounds of garbage, potholed roads and sewage spills: grim conditions like these led voters near Johannesburg to abandon their long-time loyalty to the African National Congress and hand the rival Democratic Alliance its first black township ward in South Africa, highlighting frustration over municipal-level failures ahead of November's local elections.
